envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-export-schema-note
type: schema
id: note
context: lib/node-schemas — shared node-type schema registry
intent: null
summary: null
system: null
tags: []
exported_at: 1789200000700
source: nexus.lib.node-export
payload:
  status: REAL
  source: >-
    Found while mapping intelligence and re-checking for a missed type after being asked directly.
    Doubly grounded, not a guess: intelligence/schemas.js's own real agent_notes JAA table
    ({uuid, agent, body, kind, source, relatesTo, createdAt, updatedAt, supersedes}), and
    lib/agent-tools/tools/coordination/agent-notes.js's real 'agent_notes' tool, same field set,
    independently. This is a genuinely missed 33rd type from the earlier passes — none of the 32
    covers an agent-authored, editable, supersedable note about another real thing (an agent, a
    tool, a constraint). Also the real target of copilot's own 'note' intent (see schema.intent),
    which dispatches to cortex's push-recall mechanism — not fully verified as the identical shape,
    flagged rather than assumed.
  fields:
    uuid:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real note id
    agent:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real, which agent this note is about or was authored by
    body:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real, specific note text — a lesson, workaround, or constraint, not a vague comment
    kind:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real enum — 'token-limit' | 'workaround' | 'constraint' | 'persistence' | 'other'
    source:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: real, who/what discovered this
    relatesTo:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: real, a file/component/tool this note concerns
    supersedes:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: real, uuid of an older note this one corrects — notes are editable/supersedable, not append-only-blind
    createdAt:
      type: number
      required: true
      description: real creation timestamp
    updatedAt:
      type: number
      required: false
      description: real last-update timestamp
